    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe logic itself sits in the right place and follows the file's established idiom well: it's a `@Named` `default` derivation method next to the other `formatX` helpers, it reuses `formatLocality(owner)` rather than re-parsing the customer code (mirroring how `formatMembershipLevel` builds on `formatMembershipPoints`), and the `REGION_TIMEZONE` table is cleanly extracted as a named constant. No duplication, not a catch-all \u2014 the substance is good.\n\nOne concrete, actionable idiom nit:\n\n- **Fully-qualified `java.util.Map` instead of an import.** The file already imports its other `java.util` types (`import java.util.Collection;`, `import java.util.List;`), so the inline `java.util.Map<String, String>` / `java.util.Map.of(...)` breaks the file's own convention and reads awkwardly. Add `import java.util.Map;` and use the short names (`Map<String, String> REGION_TIMEZONE = Map.of(...)`) to match the surrounding style.",
